        <subsubsection xml:id="fractran">
            <title>Intro to FRACTRAN</title>

            <p>
                Ever heard of FRACTRAN? It's a Turing-complete esoteric programming language developed by John Conway, built entirely using fractions. My writeup covering basic FRACTRAN can be found <url href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/15zQY3kjLBzO67T0lvAPYP4NhspDzJ3o4/view?usp=drivesdk">here</url>.
            </p>
            
        </subsubsection>

    <subsubsection xml:id="pwnhub">
        <title>PWNHUB</title>

        <p>
            A capture the flag style tournament I conducted where participants had to navigate clues in an Ubuntu box and finally email us the key they retrieved. The write-ups are on the Évariste club website.
        </p>
        
    </subsubsection>

